{:id :EACL-FORMAL-003
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :property
 :seed-or-trace "eacl.bench.pagination-test/permission-check-benchmark"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :availability
 :affected-versions ["current worktree at discovery"]
 :affected-backends [:datomic]
 :root-cause
 "The Datomic authenticated-store adapter labeled every signed shared-cache envelope :authenticated-v3 in the weighted provider. This erased the semantic cache kind, bypassing configured per-kind capacity and two-hit admission policies."
 :fix
 "authenticated-store first passed the semantic kind through to the weighted provider (with :authenticated-v3 only as a compatibility fallback); trusted-surface-hygiene 11.1 then deleted the adapter outright — its only consumer was the write-only :shared-cache-store option nothing read — so the defective surface no longer exists to regress."
 :closing-evidence
 ["eacl.datomic.trusted-surface-audit-test/deleted-trusted-surfaces-stay-deleted-test"
  "eacl.bench.pagination-test/permission-check-benchmark"]}
